#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:128
msgid "Hook types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:130
msgid ""
"Each hook can be tapped with one or several functions. How they are "
"executed depends on the hook type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:132
msgid ""
"Basic hook (without “Waterfall”, “Bail” or “Loop” in its name). This hook"
" simply calls every function it tapped in a row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:134
msgid ""
"__Waterfall__. A waterfall hook also calls each tapped function in a row."
" Unlike the basic hook, it passes a return value from each function to "
"the next function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:136
msgid ""
"__Bail__. A bail hook allows exiting early. When any of the tapped "
"function returns anything, the bail hook will stop executing the "
"remaining ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:138
msgid "__Loop__. TODO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:140
msgid ""
"Additionally, hooks can be synchronous or asynchronous. To reflect this, "
"there’re “Sync”, “AsyncSeries”, and “AsyncParallel” hook classes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:142
msgid ""
"__Sync__. A sync hook can only be tapped with synchronous functions "
"(using `myHook.tap()`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:144
msgid ""
"__AsyncSeries__. An async-series hook can be tapped with synchronous, "
"callback-based and promise-based functions (using `myHook.tap()`, "
"`myHook.tapAsync()` and `myHook.tapPromise()`). They call each async "
"method in a row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:146
msgid ""
"__AsyncParallel__. An async-parallel hook can also be tapped with "
"synchronous, callback-based and promise-based functions (using "
"`myHook.tap()`, `myHook.tapAsync()` and `myHook.tapPromise()`). However, "
"they run each async method in parallel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:148
msgid ""
"The hook type is reflected in its class name. E.g., "
"`AsyncSeriesWaterfallHook` allows asynchronous functions and runs them in"
" series, passing each function’s return value into the next function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:151
msgid "Interception"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:153
msgid "All Hooks offer an additional interception API:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:168
msgid ""
"**call**: `(...args) => void` Adding `call` to your interceptor will "
"trigger when hooks are triggered. You have access to the hooks arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:170
msgid ""
"**tap**: `(tap: Tap) => void` Adding `tap` to your interceptor will "
"trigger when a plugin taps into a hook. Provided is the `Tap` object. "
"`Tap` object can't be changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:172
msgid ""
"**loop**: `(...args) => void` Adding `loop` to your interceptor will "
"trigger for each loop of a looping hook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:174
msgid ""
"**register**: `(tap: Tap) => Tap | undefined` Adding `register` to your "
"interceptor will trigger for each added `Tap` and allows to modify it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:176
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tapable_README.md:178
msgid ""
"Plugins and interceptors can opt-in to access an optional `context` "
"object, which can be used to pass arbitrary values to subsequent plugins "
"and interceptors."
msgstr ""

